#N canvas 20 20 7000 9820 12;
#X text 20 20 phase9-bench -- the Phase 9 acceptance run: the mode-dependent map \, both output devices and the SP-404 in both directions. MOST OF PHASE 9 IS PROVEN HEADLESSLY -- tools/phase9-assert.sh asserts all sixteen pads \, the rate limiter and the allowlist guard in about eight seconds. What is left here is only what HARDWARE can show: a real pad under a real finger \, and a Volca you can hear. STEPPED BY HAND: press GO to run the step that has just been described \, press GO again to describe the next one. Nothing moves until you ask it to \, so the PASS IF is on screen and STILL while you read it. The prompt line always says what the next press will do., f 120;
#X text 20 150 GO ON THE MAC: the bng below \, or the dev panel's ENCODER CLICK -- u_mother-stub sends encbut unconditionally and nothing in Cut It consumes it. TURNING the encoder repeats the current step without advancing \, which is what to do when you looked away., f 120;
#X text 2400 200 ⚠️ GO ON THE DEVICE IS NOT THE ENCODER -- IT IS netcat \, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS NOT OPTIONAL. mother only forwards encbut once a patch has asked with /enableEncoder \, and NOTHING IN Cut It EVER ASKS -- m_organelle leaves the encoder out on purpose. So the click that drives this bench on the Mac is silently dead on the Organelle. Send instead with ./tools/go.sh from the Mac. ⚠️ NOT netcat: the one-liner this file used to print here does nothing on macOS -- BSD nc exits before the datagram is flushed at -w0 \, and -w1 was measured to fail too \, while the port IS bound and the bench is fine. It looks exactly like a dead bench. The device cannot send to itself either: busybox here has no nc at all. Asking mother to enable the encoder is NOT the fix either: that means writing to oscOut \, and g_oled is its sole owner., f 120;
#X text 20 280 Load it as a THIRD patch after mother.pd and main.pd. It touches nothing in the deployed patch -- it only pushes onto the same buses a controller would. A PASS IF is printed for EVERY step including the ones whose correct result is that nothing happens \, which are otherwise impossible to mark off., f 120;
#X text 2400 20 ON THE MAC EVERY ERROR STEP ALSO PRINTS /sdcard/cut-it-err.cur: write failed \, AND THAT IS NOT A FAILED STEP. u_err keeps its durable log on the Organelle's SD card \, which no Mac has -- so the write is attempted and refused every time. It is in fact the only proof off-device that the logging path ran at all. On the device that line must NOT appear \, and if it does the card is unwritable and the log is being lost silently., f 120;
#X obj 6000 40 r \$0-say;
#X obj 6000 100 print;
#X text 20 360 GO -- click here \, or the dev panel's encoder button. MAC ONLY -- on the device use netcat \, top right., f 60;
#X obj 20 420 bng 40 250 50 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1;
#X obj 20 500 s \$0-go;
#X obj 300 420 r encbut;
#X obj 300 480 select 1;
#X obj 300 540 t b;
#X obj 300 600 s \$0-go;
#X text 560 480 encbut sends 1 THEN 0 \, so select 1 is what stops one press counting twice., f 46;
#X obj 300 680 netreceive 9998 1;
#X obj 300 740 route go;
#X obj 300 800 t b;
#X obj 300 860 s \$0-go;
#X obj 1400 420 r enc;
#X obj 1400 480 t b;
#X obj 1400 540 s \$0-repeat;
#X text 1660 480 enc is 1 for up and 0 for down -- not plus or minus one -- so either direction repeats., f 46;
#X text 20 920 THE STATE MACHINE. phase 0 means the step has been described and not yet run \; phase 1 means it has run. SETTING THE STEP NUMBER IS WHAT DESCRIBES IT \, so advancing is just an increment -- there is no second path to keep in step., f 120;
#X obj 20 980 r \$0-go;
#X obj 20 1040 f;
#X obj 20 1100 select 0 1;
#X obj 300 1040 r \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 20 1170 t b b;
#X msg 300 1230 1;
#X obj 300 1290 s \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 20 1290 f;
#X obj 20 1350 s \$0-do-run;
#X obj 900 1170 t b b;
#X msg 1180 1230 0;
#X obj 1180 1290 s \$0-set-phase;
#X obj 900 1350 f;
#X obj 900 1410 + 1;
#X obj 900 1470 s \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1700 980 r \$0-set-step;
#X obj 1700 1040 t f f f;
#X obj 1700 1110 s \$0-set-inc;
#X obj 1980 1110 s \$0-set-run;
#X obj 1180 1350 r \$0-set-inc;
#X obj 300 1410 r \$0-set-run;
#X obj 2260 1110 s \$0-do-show;
#X obj 2100 980 r \$0-repeat;
#X obj 2100 1040 s \$0-do-show;
#X obj 2500 980 loadbang;
#X obj 2500 1040 del 500;
#X msg 2500 1100 1;
#X obj 2500 1160 s \$0-set-step;
#X text 20 1920 DESCRIBING A STEP. One select per step rather than one wide fan \, so every cord stays short and local -- the same reason u_map chains its routes., f 120;
#X obj 20 2020 r \$0-do-show;
#X obj 20 2080 select 1;
#X obj 240 2080 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2080 === STEP-01-of-14 === baseline -- read the OLED footer before touching anything;
#X msg 700 2130 PASS IF: the footer reads 57 BPM and NOT 120 -- this is a REAL TEST and not a formality -- knobs.txt holds knob 1 at about 0.096 and mother pushes it at boot. 57 means the message went through the mapping TABLE and came out the tempo handler. 120 means u_tempo is sitting on its own default and the table never matched. Also note which mode lamp is lit on the Launchpad top row -- a restored session comes up wherever you left it;
#X msg 700 2180 >>> press GO to run step 1 of 14;
#X obj 240 2250 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2340 select 2;
#X obj 240 2340 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2340 === STEP-02-of-14 === GET TO MODE 1 -- HANDS -- press transport key 1 on the nanoKONTROL;
#X msg 700 2390 PASS IF: the lit lamp moves to the first position. Fader 1 is only bound in mode 1 so the later steps need this. If the lamp does not move then the nano is not reaching param and nothing below will work;
#X msg 700 2440 >>> press GO to run step 2 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 2510 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2600 select 3;
#X obj 240 2600 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2600 === STEP-03-of-14 === THE 404 RECEIVE SIDE -- HANDS -- select BANK A on the SP-404 and press pad 1;
#X msg 700 2650 PASS IF: the OLED shows sp-hit and the number 1 -- this is the map this project got WRONG once and pad 1 is note 48 -- ⚠️ STATE WHICH BANK IS SELECTED OUT LOUD before every one of these: the 404 lights only the bank it is on and a receive test that does not state the bank cost half an hour once;
#X msg 700 2700 >>> press GO to run step 3 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 2770 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 2860 select 4;
#X obj 240 2860 t b b b;
#X msg 700 2860 === STEP-04-of-14 === THE PAD THAT BREAKS THE OLD FORMULA -- HANDS -- press pad 5 on bank A;
#X msg 700 2910 PASS IF: the OLED shows sp-hit and the number 5 -- pad 5 is note 44 and NOT note 52 -- anything other than 5 means the pad table is wrong in exactly the direction this repo used to have it wrong;
#X msg 700 2960 >>> press GO to run step 4 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 3030 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3120 select 5;
#X obj 240 3120 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3120 === STEP-05-of-14 === WALK THE WHOLE BANK -- HANDS -- press pads 1 through 16 in order on bank A;
#X msg 700 3170 PASS IF: the OLED counts 1 2 3 up to 16 in step with your finger. The headless gate already asserts all sixteen notes -- what this adds is that the DEVICE agrees with it. A run that goes 1 2 3 4 then jumps is the old formula surviving somewhere;
#X msg 700 3220 >>> press GO to run step 5 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 3290 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3380 select 6;
#X obj 240 3380 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3380 === STEP-06-of-14 === THE BANK IS THE CHANNEL -- HANDS -- select BANK B and press pad 1;
#X msg 700 3430 PASS IF: the OLED STILL shows sp-hit and the number 1 -- the bank is deliberately not on the display because the 404 shows its own bank on its own screen. An UNCHANGED reading is the pass here;
#X msg 700 3480 >>> press GO to run step 6 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 3550 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3640 select 7;
#X obj 240 3640 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3640 === STEP-07-of-14 === A RELEASE IS NOT A PRESS -- HANDS -- press and hold any pad then let go;
#X msg 700 3690 PASS IF: the OLED updates on the PRESS and does NOT update again on the release. The release is a real event and does reach param but it is not worth a display row. Two updates per hit means the velocity test on the disp side has gone;
#X msg 700 3740 >>> press GO to run step 7 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 3810 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 3900 select 8;
#X obj 240 3900 t b b b;
#X msg 700 3900 === STEP-08-of-14 === THE MAP IS MODE-DEPENDENT -- HANDS -- in mode 1 move FADER 1 on the nanoKONTROL;
#X msg 700 3950 PASS IF: the Volca tone changes as you move it. Fader 1 is bound to Volca CC 41 in mode 1 and to NOTHING in the other five. THIS IS THE POINT OF THE WHOLE PHASE -- a control means whatever the row for the current mode says it means. ⚠️ The Volca is BY EAR and always will be -- it transmits nothing so there is never a readback;
#X msg 700 4000 >>> press GO to run step 8 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 4070 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4160 select 9;
#X obj 240 4160 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4160 === STEP-09-of-14 === NOW CHANGE MODE AND MOVE THE SAME FADER -- HANDS -- transport key 4 then fader 1;
#X msg 700 4210 PASS IF: the Volca does NOT change. Nothing is broken -- there is no row for fader 1 in mode 4 and an unmapped control is the normal state of most controls. SILENCE IS THE PASS. The OLED still shows the fader moving because m_nano publishes it either way;
#X msg 700 4260 >>> press GO to run step 9 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 4330 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4420 select 10;
#X obj 240 4420 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4420 === STEP-10-of-14 === AND BACK -- HANDS -- transport key 1 then fader 1 again;
#X msg 700 4470 PASS IF: the Volca responds again. If it stays silent then the mode did not change back and the lit lamp will say so;
#X msg 700 4520 >>> press GO to run step 10 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 4590 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4680 select 11;
#X obj 240 4680 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4680 === STEP-11-of-14 === TEMPO STILL COMES FROM KNOB 1 -- HANDS -- turn Organelle knob 1;
#X msg 700 4730 PASS IF: the footer BPM follows the knob over roughly 10 to 500 -- ⚠️ THE FIRST TOUCH WILL JUMP -- knobs.txt restored the value but the physical knob is wherever you left it. That is expected and it is the case for parameter pickup. Knob 1 is a TABLE ROW now like everything else;
#X msg 700 4780 >>> press GO to run step 11 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 4850 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 4940 select 12;
#X obj 240 4940 t b b b;
#X msg 700 4940 === STEP-12-of-14 === THE TRANSPORT STILL WORKS -- HANDS -- press the Organelle aux button twice;
#X msg 700 4990 PASS IF: the aux LED changes state each press and the footer agrees. The transport migrated into the table too so this is the proof that migrating it did not quietly drop it;
#X msg 700 5040 >>> press GO to run step 12 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 5110 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5200 select 13;
#X obj 240 5200 t b b b;
#X msg 700 5200 === STEP-13-of-14 === PANIC HAS A CONTROL AT LAST -- HANDS -- hold a pad on bank B then press nano bottom-row button 8;
#X msg 700 5250 PASS IF: nothing is left sounding. ⚠️ NOTHING ON THE DEVICE COULD RAISE PANIC BEFORE THIS PHASE -- only the Mac dev panel could -- so this row is new and the button choice is a suggestion you can move in one line of cut-it-map.txt. u_tempo used to silence bank A alone which is one tenth of the instrument;
#X msg 700 5300 >>> press GO to run step 13 of 14 -- THIS ONE NEEDS YOUR HANDS ON THE HARDWARE;
#X obj 240 5370 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5460 select 14;
#X obj 240 5460 t b b b;
#X msg 700 5460 === STEP-14-of-14 === END MARKER -- not a test -- the run is over;
#X msg 700 5510 PASS IF: nothing further prints. THIS STEP ASSERTS NOTHING. ⚠️ Every step above is HANDS-ON and has NO actions -- so this bench never has to be LOADED on the device which means no killall pd and no stranded Launchpad. Read the steps and press the real controls. The logic is proven headlessly by tools/phase9-assert.sh;
#X msg 700 5560 >>> press GO to run step 14 of 14;
#X obj 240 5630 s \$0-say;
#X obj 20 5720 t b;
#X msg 240 5720 === BENCH COMPLETE === every step has been run -- reload the patch to go round again;
#X obj 240 5780 s \$0-say;
#X text 20 5860 RUNNING A STEP. The actions fire in the order they are listed -- rightmost trigger outlet first -- and the line saying the step has fired goes out LAST \, off outlet 0 \, so it cannot arrive before the thing it describes., f 120;
#X obj 20 5960 r \$0-do-run;
